\chapter{Assembly}

This is the only file with \texttt{@@o} directives. The concept chapters never
name an output path; they define chunks, and the assembly routes those chunks
to the layer-oriented files the C toolchain expects. Because routing lives
here alone, the physical layout can change --- split a file, rename a
directory --- without touching a single concept narrative.

The store and its header:

@o src/accounts.h
@{@<Accounts: header@>
@}

@o src/accounts.c
@{@<Accounts: implementation@>
@}

The ledger and its header:

@o src/ledger.h
@{@<Ledger: header@>
@}

@o src/ledger.c
@{@<Ledger: implementation@>
@}

The command-line surface:

@o src/main.c
@{@<Api: main@>
@}
